WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Advertise your product or brand here
contact www.OpenSubtitles.org today

2
00:00:33.783 --> 00:00:40.665
A SHOP FOR KILLERS

3
00:00:43.668 --> 00:00:46.004
EPISODE 2
JEONG JINMAN. JEONG JINMAN. JEONG JINMAN

4
00:00:48.882 --> 00:00:50.884
Are you
out of your freaking mind?

5
00:00:54.888 --> 00:00:57.057
Mom passed away so suddenly.

6
00:00:58.808 --> 00:01:00.894
There's something strange about it.

7
00:01:03.354 --> 00:01:04.439
I think

8
00:01:05.023 --> 00:01:06.232
we should do an autopsy.

9
00:01:07.192 --> 00:01:08.276
An autopsy?

10
00:01:10.153 --> 00:01:11.154
Jinman.

11
00:01:12.322 --> 00:01:15.992
Mom had surgery
for biliary tract cancer twice.

12
00:01:16.743 --> 00:01:18.411
She suffered for over five years.

13
00:01:18.995 --> 00:01:22.082
The doctor even told us
to prepare for the worst.

14
00:01:22.957 --> 00:01:25.835
She regained energy briefly
because her son she thought was dead

15
00:01:26.503 --> 00:01:31.091
came back after eight years.
Her death wasn't sudden.

16
00:01:32.342 --> 00:01:33.426
Are you sure?

17
00:01:34.552 --> 00:01:35.970
What if I'm not?

18
00:01:37.388 --> 00:01:38.389
What?

19
00:01:39.057 --> 00:01:42.644
Do you want to play
a loving son or something now?

20
00:01:43.812 --> 00:01:46.981
Do you want the whole neighborhood to know
you two don't get along?

21
00:01:47.065 --> 00:01:48.608
Why are you yelling?

22
00:01:48.691 --> 00:01:51.611
There's no time for this.
We have a lot to do.

23
00:01:56.032 --> 00:01:58.618
Jeong Jian!

24
00:01:59.202 --> 00:02:02.288
I told you to stay still!

25
00:02:02.831 --> 00:02:04.207
Oh. no. What do we do?

26
00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:07.585
Come here.

27
00:02:11.923 --> 00:02:14.217
-Jinman.
-Yes?

28
00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:18.138
We'll take care of the preparations here.
Why don't you go home with Jian?

29
00:02:18.805 --> 00:02:21.558
Jian is of no help here.

30
00:02:49.544 --> 00:02:51.212
Please attain enlightenment.

31
00:03:01.598 --> 00:03:05.059
Your mother worried so much about her sons
when she was alive.

32
00:03:05.935 --> 00:03:07.353
It must be so hard for you.

33
00:03:09.856 --> 00:03:12.317
I'm sorry. but who are you?

34
00:03:12.942 --> 00:03:14.485
You don't remember me?

35
00:03:15.695 --> 00:03:19.699
I'm an old friend of Jinman's.

36
00:03:19.782 --> 00:03:21.701
-Oh. I see.
-Yes.

37
00:03:22.452 --> 00:03:25.079
But I don't see Jinman.

38
00:04:22.470 --> 00:04:23.930
Then...

39
00:04:24.013 --> 00:04:27.725
now that Grandma's dead.
we can't see her anymore?

40
00:04:33.064 --> 00:04:34.107
No.

41
00:04:35.692 --> 00:04:36.901
Not anymore.

42
00:04:40.613 --> 00:04:43.157
Dying sucks.

43
00:04:45.326 --> 00:04:47.370
You're right. It sucks.

44
00:04:50.206 --> 00:04:51.291
But...

45
00:04:52.375 --> 00:04:54.252
we all die eventually.

46
00:04:55.003 --> 00:04:57.964
Death isn't something scary.

47
00:05:02.468 --> 00:05:03.886
Do you see that lion?

48
00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:07.098
That lion will die soon.

49
00:05:09.559 --> 00:05:10.685
But take a look.

50
00:05:11.436 --> 00:05:13.938
The lion who's facing death is quiet

51
00:05:15.023 --> 00:05:16.399
while they're all loud.

52
00:05:20.528 --> 00:05:21.779
Why do you think that is?

53
00:05:27.035 --> 00:05:28.703
Only the weak bark.

54
00:05:30.955 --> 00:05:32.290
The strong don't.

55
00:05:33.916 --> 00:05:35.251
You must become strong.

56
00:05:38.338 --> 00:05:41.674
To make your opponent bark.

57
00:05:46.512 --> 00:05:47.680
I'm scared.

58
00:05:48.514 --> 00:05:49.724
Don't be scared.

59
00:05:51.642 --> 00:05:52.810
Whatever makes you scared.

60
00:05:53.728 --> 00:05:56.064
keep your eyes open and face it.

61
00:06:04.489 --> 00:06:06.824
Why aren't you answering it? Isn't it Mom?

62
00:06:12.622 --> 00:06:13.664
Who is it?

63
00:06:15.875 --> 00:06:17.668
How did you get this number?

64
00:06:39.732 --> 00:06:42.151
Listen up. Jian.

65
00:06:43.069 --> 00:06:46.197
I'm going to the funeral hall
to meet Mom and Dad.

66
00:06:46.280 --> 00:06:48.366
You have to stay at home alone.

67
00:06:48.950 --> 00:06:51.828
My friend will come
and ask you to open the door.

68
00:06:52.370 --> 00:06:55.790
But don't just open the door for him.

69
00:06:55.873 --> 00:06:57.792
Give him a riddle.

70
00:06:57.875 --> 00:07:00.711
Open the door only if he solves it.

71
00:07:01.712 --> 00:07:03.297
If he doesn't know the answer.

72
00:07:04.799 --> 00:07:05.967
don't open the door.

73
00:07:06.676 --> 00:07:07.760
Can you do that?

74
00:07:08.344 --> 00:07:10.304
Yes. I can do it.

75
00:07:11.222 --> 00:07:13.433
And I want to give him this riddle.

76
00:07:13.516 --> 00:07:15.685
"What is a horse's favorite sport?"

77
00:07:18.479 --> 00:07:19.564
"Stable tennis."

78
00:07:28.114 --> 00:07:29.323
Jeong Jinman!

79
00:07:32.869 --> 00:07:34.537
Will you be right back?

80
00:07:40.877 --> 00:07:43.296
Yes. I'll be right back.

81
00:07:50.219 --> 00:07:56.976
HAENGUN MANSION

82
00:08:17.538 --> 00:08:18.998
Are you my uncle's friend?

83
00:09:00.665 --> 00:09:04.544
I can't just open the door.
I'll give you a riddle.

84
00:09:04.627 --> 00:09:07.588
I'll open the door if you solve it.

85
00:09:07.672 --> 00:09:10.007
What is a horse's favorite sport?

86
00:09:13.469 --> 00:09:16.013
Solve the riddle.

87
00:09:16.097 --> 00:09:18.766
What is a horse's favorite sport?

88
00:09:24.897 --> 00:09:28.276
What is a horse's favorite sport...

89
00:09:49.755 --> 00:09:52.008
Are you really my uncle's friend?

90
00:10:33.215 --> 00:10:35.176
STABLE TENNIS

91
00:10:44.560 --> 00:10:46.771
I'M YOUR UNCLE'S FRIEND. SORRY I'M LATE.

92
00:11:02.953 --> 00:11:06.248
CAN YOU WAIT IN YOUR ROOM FOR A MINUTE?

93
00:12:07.650 --> 00:12:09.777
Fuck. my teeth.

94
00:12:20.730 --> 00:12:22.941
Attain enlightenment. you bastard!

95
00:12:39.457 --> 00:12:42.335
- Are you sure she's in here?
- I saw the door close.

96
00:12:57.266 --> 00:13:00.436
My goodness. I'm so exhausted.

97
00:13:01.020 --> 00:13:03.439
Good grief.

98
00:13:21.040 --> 00:13:22.166
What the hell?

99
00:13:25.837 --> 00:13:26.921
Wow.

100
00:13:28.423 --> 00:13:29.424
Huh?

101
00:13:29.924 --> 00:13:31.426
I can tell.

102
00:13:31.509 --> 00:13:33.928
You're definitely Jeong Jinman's niece.

103
00:13:34.595 --> 00:13:38.307
You'll get seriously hurt
if you fall from there. kid.

104
00:13:38.391 --> 00:13:41.019
You might die or become crippled.

105
00:13:41.853 --> 00:13:43.896
So stop that and come up to me.

106
00:13:44.772 --> 00:13:46.649
Okay? Come on!

107
00:13:54.824 --> 00:13:55.825
No!

108
00:14:08.046 --> 00:14:11.090
Goodness. The apple doesn't fall
far from the tree.

109
00:14:26.189 --> 00:14:27.356
Oh. my goodness!

110
00:14:39.535 --> 00:14:42.163
I think we're in a bit of a jam.

111
00:14:52.381 --> 00:14:54.383
So she's the daughter of the couple

112
00:14:54.467 --> 00:14:56.427
murdered at Boram Funeral Home?

113
00:14:57.011 --> 00:14:58.262
That's right.

114
00:14:59.263 --> 00:15:01.349
Her parents didn't return home

115
00:15:01.432 --> 00:15:03.392
after what happened at the funeral.

116
00:15:03.976 --> 00:15:07.271
so she left to go find them by herself
and got into an accident.

117
00:15:07.980 --> 00:15:09.065
Goodness.

118
00:15:09.524 --> 00:15:11.943
Then what happens to her now?

119
00:15:12.026 --> 00:15:13.402
Well...

120
00:15:13.486 --> 00:15:15.947
She has an uncle.

121
00:15:16.030 --> 00:15:18.741
-Yes.
-But he's been missing for years.

122
00:15:19.283 --> 00:15:21.911
And his social security number
was canceled last year.

123
00:17:34.168 --> 00:17:37.713
JEONG JIAN

124
00:19:06.635 --> 00:19:08.846
INSTRUCTIONS FOR MORGUE USE

125
00:19:10.389 --> 00:19:12.308
RESTRICTED AREA
AUTHORIZED PERSONNEL ONLY

126
00:19:14.643 --> 00:19:16.687
MORGUE

127
00:19:39.126 --> 00:19:40.669
I think I found her.

128
00:19:41.379 --> 00:19:43.923
I'll take care of her and bring her out.
Stand by.

129
00:20:26.882 --> 00:20:28.175
Mommy?

130
00:21:23.898 --> 00:21:26.484
What are you doing here?
I told you to stand by.

131
00:23:20.905 --> 00:23:22.240
Close your eyes. Jian.

132
00:23:24.409 --> 00:23:25.660
Let's go home now.

133
00:23:34.127 --> 00:23:36.921
ONE MONTH LATER

134
00:25:00.213 --> 00:25:01.214
Get out.

135
00:25:34.372 --> 00:25:35.540
Listen up. Jian.

136
00:25:37.458 --> 00:25:39.252
I'm not your parent.

137
00:25:39.919 --> 00:25:41.045
And I can never be.

138
00:25:41.629 --> 00:25:42.630
Which means

139
00:25:43.381 --> 00:25:45.466
I can't do the things

140
00:25:46.175 --> 00:25:48.052
your parents did for you.

141
00:26:42.297 --> 00:26:46.009
<i>It appears to be aphasia</i>
<i>coupled with dissociative amnesia.</i>

142
00:26:46.510 --> 00:26:48.637
<i>It doesn't seem to be a physical problem.</i>

143
00:26:49.471 --> 00:26:51.223
<i>She lost both of her parents.</i>

144
00:26:51.306 --> 00:26:55.143
<i>I think the resulting shock</i>
<i>and post-traumatic stress caused it.</i>

145
00:26:55.894 --> 00:26:59.272
<i>Let's see what happens</i>
<i>with medication and counseling.</i>

146
00:28:08.466 --> 00:28:10.927
There's no big problem with her studies.

147
00:28:11.720 --> 00:28:14.389
but since Jian can't speak.

148
00:28:15.181 --> 00:28:17.601
it's causing some difficulties.

149
00:28:21.980 --> 00:28:24.482
She's stupid.
She still can't say anything.

150
00:28:24.566 --> 00:28:26.693
Hey. can you really not speak?

151
00:28:26.776 --> 00:28:29.029
- She's always like that.
- She's a mute.

152
00:28:31.031 --> 00:28:32.282
- What's he doing?
- Wow.

153
00:28:32.365 --> 00:28:34.701
- Does he like her?
- Jeongmin. what's your deal?

154
00:28:34.784 --> 00:28:36.953
- Out of the blue?
- Are they fighting?

155
00:28:38.371 --> 00:28:39.456
Are you okay?

156
00:28:46.671 --> 00:28:47.672
Did you know?

157
00:28:47.797 --> 00:28:49.007
- What?
- What is it?

158
00:28:49.090 --> 00:28:50.091
That dummy's mom

159
00:28:50.592 --> 00:28:52.218
was stabbed to death by her dad.

160
00:28:52.302 --> 00:28:53.428
- Why?
- What?

161
00:28:53.511 --> 00:28:55.305
- Why?
- She was having an affair.

162
00:28:57.724 --> 00:29:01.061
Her dad jumped off the roof
of the funeral home and killed himself.

163
00:29:01.144 --> 00:29:03.855
- Really? Suicide?
- Ask your mom.

164
00:29:03.939 --> 00:29:06.775
Everyone in Yecheong knows.

165
00:29:06.858 --> 00:29:07.943
That's crazy!

166
00:29:10.695 --> 00:29:13.239
- Hey. are you okay!
- Hey!

167
00:29:13.990 --> 00:29:15.909
- Are you okay?
- Oh. no.

168
00:29:15.992 --> 00:29:18.828
She can't seem to blend in
with the other kids.

169
00:29:18.912 --> 00:29:20.872
I can see she's an outsider.

170
00:29:22.457 --> 00:29:23.458
Dad!

171
00:29:23.541 --> 00:29:24.584
Mom!

172
00:29:24.668 --> 00:29:27.212
Why are you so late? I'm soaked!

173
00:29:27.295 --> 00:29:29.965
Jiyun. did you have fun today?

174
00:29:32.467 --> 00:29:33.551
Wait for me!

175
00:29:34.344 --> 00:29:36.304
Hey! Wait up!

176
00:29:43.979 --> 00:29:46.147
Hey. Shinae! Let's go together.

177
00:29:46.856 --> 00:29:49.025
Mom!

178
00:29:49.109 --> 00:29:50.443
YECHEONG ELEMENTARY SCHOOL

179
00:29:50.527 --> 00:29:53.154
Hey! Wait up!

180
00:31:17.045 --> 00:31:20.841
You're treating Jian for aphasia. right?

181
00:32:24.863 --> 00:32:26.406
PROTRACTOR
5.000 WON

182
00:32:27.532 --> 00:32:28.742
PROTRACTOR
5.000 WON

183
00:32:30.577 --> 00:32:31.578
CLAY
10.000 WON

184
00:32:34.039 --> 00:32:35.123
RECORDER
20.000 WON

185
00:32:35.207 --> 00:32:36.208
TRIANGLE
30.000 WON

186
00:32:37.334 --> 00:32:38.752
TRIANGLE
30.000 WON

187
00:32:42.673 --> 00:32:44.299
CASTANETS
40.000 WON

188
00:32:54.518 --> 00:32:55.936
I understand

189
00:32:56.687 --> 00:32:59.022
what you're trying to say.

190
00:32:59.106 --> 00:33:00.107
However...

191
00:33:01.900 --> 00:33:03.068
I think this problem

192
00:33:04.403 --> 00:33:07.239
is something Jian must overcome
on her own.

193
00:33:16.832 --> 00:33:18.166
It's the crazy mute's fault.

194
00:33:19.084 --> 00:33:20.252
So unlucky.

195
00:33:23.171 --> 00:33:24.172
Yeah.

196
00:33:24.756 --> 00:33:25.841
Hey. shut it.

197
00:33:32.973 --> 00:33:34.099
Let's go.

198
00:35:04.106 --> 00:35:05.190
Jeong...

199
00:35:06.525 --> 00:35:07.526
Jin...

200
00:35:07.609 --> 00:35:08.693
man...

201
00:35:13.281 --> 00:35:15.575
Jeong Jinman!

202
00:35:17.452 --> 00:35:19.413
Jeong Jinman!

203
00:35:20.622 --> 00:35:22.666
Jeong Jinman!

204
00:35:25.836 --> 00:35:27.629
Jeong Jinman!

205
00:35:31.425 --> 00:35:33.260
Jeong Jinman!

206
00:35:48.574 --> 00:35:51.702
Why did you come so late?
You said you'd be right back!

207
00:35:51.786 --> 00:35:55.122
Why did you come so late? Why?

208
00:36:01.545 --> 00:36:02.755
I'm sorry I'm late.

209
00:36:04.799 --> 00:36:05.883
Jeong Jian.

210
00:36:50.386 --> 00:36:51.429
Come here.

211
00:36:52.263 --> 00:36:53.347
Let's eat together.

212
00:37:29.008 --> 00:37:30.593
This pork belly's good.

213
00:38:04.126 --> 00:38:07.088
Your front door was open. so I came in.

214
00:38:20.142 --> 00:38:21.560
If it's all right with you.

215
00:38:21.644 --> 00:38:24.313
can I wait for him inside?

216
00:38:27.316 --> 00:38:31.445
My uncle said he wasn't coming home today.

217
00:38:31.529 --> 00:38:33.447
So you should just go back.

218
00:38:34.073 --> 00:38:35.574
I'll tell my uncle

219
00:38:35.658 --> 00:38:37.493
to call you later.

220
00:38:43.749 --> 00:38:45.209
You're the niece

221
00:38:45.292 --> 00:38:47.336
that attends
Gongju National University. right?

222
00:38:47.962 --> 00:38:51.090
Your uncle bragged
about how pretty and smart you are.

223
00:38:59.306 --> 00:39:02.101
I'm not smart or pretty.

224
00:39:02.852 --> 00:39:05.104
I don't attend
Gongju National University. either.

225
00:39:05.813 --> 00:39:08.149
My uncle would never say that.

226
00:39:12.862 --> 00:39:14.864
Do you really know my uncle?

227
00:39:18.451 --> 00:39:19.910
I understand.

228
00:39:19.994 --> 00:39:23.372
I'll call your uncle
and come back next time.

229
00:39:49.815 --> 00:39:52.109
DON'T LET ANYONE ELSE KILL YOU

230
00:39:52.193 --> 00:39:54.820
I'LL COME AND KILL YOU MYSELF. JIAN.

231
00:39:54.904 --> 00:39:56.155
Jian.

232
00:39:56.238 --> 00:39:57.490
Come and look at this.

233
00:39:58.199 --> 00:40:01.619
I hacked into the operator's account
for murthehelp and had a look.

234
00:40:02.244 --> 00:40:05.581
This website is operated
for authorized members only.

235
00:40:06.457 --> 00:40:07.541
Look.

236
00:40:10.711 --> 00:40:14.089
Members can get codes
according to their grades.

237
00:40:14.173 --> 00:40:17.218
The process is a little tricky.
but it says that only those

238
00:40:17.301 --> 00:40:18.802
who pass this can get codes.

239
00:40:19.929 --> 00:40:21.013
Codes?

240
00:40:21.096 --> 00:40:25.501
"Only authorized members with the operator's
codes can purchase items on murthehelp."

241
00:40:26.784 --> 00:40:30.121
"Not all items are available for purchase
with provided codes."

242
00:40:30.204 --> 00:40:32.040
"Each code has a different quality."

243
00:40:32.123 --> 00:40:35.251
"You can only purchase
the qualified items for that code."

244
00:40:35.877 --> 00:40:37.670
A different quality for each code?

245
00:40:38.171 --> 00:40:39.213
Yes.

246
00:40:39.881 --> 00:40:40.965
There are four codes.

247
00:40:41.424 --> 00:40:44.260
<i>People who kill people are Code Red.</i>

248
00:40:44.344 --> 00:40:47.597
<i>I think it's like contract killers</i>
<i>that we see in movies.</i>

249
00:40:48.556 --> 00:40:51.142
<i>Guns. weapons. bombs. and poisons.</i>

250
00:40:51.225 --> 00:40:54.187
It seems they can buy
items needed to kill people.

251
00:40:54.270 --> 00:40:56.105
Spies are Code Purple.

252
00:40:56.189 --> 00:40:58.775
<i>"A code for people</i>
<i>who buy and sell information."</i>

253
00:40:58.858 --> 00:41:01.027
<i>"A variety of listening devices</i>
<i>or cameras."</i>

254
00:41:01.110 --> 00:41:03.738
<i>"Simple weapons or goods that you can use</i>

255
00:41:03.821 --> 00:41:06.282
to kill yourself
when your cover is blown."

256
00:41:06.699 --> 00:41:07.950
It sounds so scary.

257
00:41:11.287 --> 00:41:12.497
Do you want to try it?

258
00:41:14.123 --> 00:41:16.000
Code Yellow is for the clean-up crew.

259
00:41:16.084 --> 00:41:20.296
<i>"Drugs. detergents. and cleaning tools</i>
<i>needed for body disposal and clean-up."</i>

260
00:41:20.380 --> 00:41:24.759
It also says that they provide various
administrative services to evade the law.

261
00:41:24.842 --> 00:41:28.304
You said there are four codes.
What's the last one?

262
00:41:28.388 --> 00:41:29.430
Code Green.

263
00:41:29.931 --> 00:41:30.932
Green?

264
00:41:31.015 --> 00:41:34.519
Yes. but unlike the other codes.
I don't think it has a category.

265
00:41:41.651 --> 00:41:42.985
Code Green.

266
00:41:43.069 --> 00:41:47.323
"Those who have received codes from
murthehelp may never attack Code Green."

267
00:41:47.407 --> 00:41:50.201
"If someone disobeys this
and attacks Code Green.

268
00:41:50.702 --> 00:41:56.624
everyone with a code must risk
their lives to protect Code Green."

269
00:41:57.834 --> 00:41:59.293
So who's Code Green?

270
00:42:02.046 --> 00:42:03.881
The operator of murthehelp.

271
00:42:04.382 --> 00:42:06.217
Your uncle. Jeong Jinman.

272
00:42:07.593 --> 00:42:08.678
And...

273
00:42:09.053 --> 00:42:10.680
code green: JEONG JINMAN. JEONG JIAN

274
00:42:12.515 --> 00:42:13.599
Jeong Jian.

275
00:42:24.068 --> 00:42:25.862
What on earth...

276
00:42:30.074 --> 00:42:31.325
Am I supposed

277
00:42:32.660 --> 00:42:33.828
to believe all this?

278
00:42:35.288 --> 00:42:36.330
Jeongmin.

279
00:42:37.498 --> 00:42:39.542
Does this make sense...

280
00:42:57.268 --> 00:42:58.311
What is this?

281
00:43:00.188 --> 00:43:02.398
What is happening?

282
00:43:12.992 --> 00:43:16.037
What... the heck is that?

283
00:43:42.855 --> 00:43:44.607
I'm not getting any signal.

284
00:43:45.858 --> 00:43:46.859
Darn it!

285
00:43:49.320 --> 00:43:50.363
Jeongmin.

286
00:43:50.446 --> 00:43:51.697
Let's use the back door!

287
00:44:06.462 --> 00:44:07.547
What's with the door?

288
00:44:08.381 --> 00:44:09.423
Is it bulletproof?

289
00:44:25.022 --> 00:44:26.107
What?

290
00:44:27.483 --> 00:44:28.693
Why aren't they moving?

291
00:44:30.194 --> 00:44:31.946
Are they out of bullets?

292
00:45:04.562 --> 00:45:05.730
What's that?

293
00:45:33.883 --> 00:45:35.259
Jeongmin. this way!

294
00:45:48.064 --> 00:45:49.315
Jeongmin!

295
00:45:55.279 --> 00:45:56.656
Shut the door!

296
00:47:23.325 --> 00:47:24.326
Jeongmin. duck!

297
00:47:40.134 --> 00:47:44.889
A SHOP FOR KILLERS

298
00:47:44.972 --> 00:47:46.098
Hello.

299
00:47:44.972 --> 00:47:46.098
Hello.

300
00:47:50.227 --> 00:47:51.395
Oh. really?

301
00:47:51.479 --> 00:47:53.272
You got married? Congrats!

302
00:47:54.648 --> 00:47:56.901
- Oh. congratulations!
- Thanks.

303
00:47:56.984 --> 00:47:59.195
But does your wife know you do this work?

304
00:47:59.278 --> 00:48:00.696
No way. That would be bad.

305
00:48:00.780 --> 00:48:04.033
By the way.
where were you from again? 707?

306
00:48:04.116 --> 00:48:05.284
No. the UDT/SEAL.

307
00:48:05.367 --> 00:48:07.661
UDT? Really?

308
00:48:10.122 --> 00:48:11.457
Mr. Kim. you're here!

309
00:48:11.540 --> 00:48:12.958
Hello!

310
00:48:13.042 --> 00:48:14.919
-Welcome!
-Hello!

311
00:48:15.002 --> 00:48:16.128
You're here as well.

312
00:48:16.629 --> 00:48:17.713
Yes. sir.

313
00:48:20.674 --> 00:48:21.926
Is married life fun?

314
00:48:22.009 --> 00:48:23.511
Not at all.

315
00:48:40.778 --> 00:48:43.280
Sir. do we have to do that?

316
00:48:44.156 --> 00:48:47.451
After today. it doesn't matter
if we have one or not anyway.

317
00:48:49.203 --> 00:48:51.330
You do what's comfortable for you.

318
00:48:51.956 --> 00:48:53.791
I don't need this code anymore.

319
00:48:53.874 --> 00:48:57.086
Wow!
The veteran warriors have all gathered!

320
00:48:58.712 --> 00:49:00.172
Victory!

321
00:49:00.464 --> 00:49:01.674
-Victory!
-Victory!

322
00:49:02.842 --> 00:49:05.427
You came. Mr. Kim.

323
00:49:05.511 --> 00:49:07.471
Seongjo. has it been a year?

324
00:49:08.639 --> 00:49:10.641
Thank you for changing your mind.

325
00:49:10.724 --> 00:49:15.020
I bet we'll finish early today
if we follow Mr. Kim's lead.

326
00:49:15.104 --> 00:49:17.690
Let's grab some <i>galbi</i> and <i>makgeolli</i> after!

327
00:49:17.773 --> 00:49:19.191
- Sounds good!
- Sure!

328
00:49:21.152 --> 00:49:22.653
What weapons did you bring?

329
00:49:22.736 --> 00:49:25.030
Bring out your babies. Come on.

330
00:49:27.616 --> 00:49:31.370
This is so worn out.

331
00:49:34.081 --> 00:49:35.541
Wow. man!

332
00:49:35.624 --> 00:49:37.543
Where did you get the rail?

333
00:49:37.626 --> 00:49:40.004
Jinman installed it for me. I feel so bad.

334
00:49:40.087 --> 00:49:41.839
I bought this from Jinman too.

335
00:49:41.922 --> 00:49:43.549
Four mags will be enough. right?

336
00:49:43.632 --> 00:49:45.551
By the way. what's up with your gun?

337
00:49:45.634 --> 00:49:49.054
I've used every gun out there.
but this is light and comfortable.

338
00:49:49.138 --> 00:49:50.472
Right. good for you.

339
00:49:51.765 --> 00:49:53.601
I feel kind of bad for Jinman.

340
00:49:54.185 --> 00:49:57.730
Fuck that. He's dead. and we're alive.
We must go on.

341
00:49:58.230 --> 00:49:59.231
All right.

342
00:49:59.315 --> 00:50:01.317
The person who captures the niece

343
00:50:01.400 --> 00:50:02.902
or kills her

344
00:50:02.985 --> 00:50:04.737
will get a fat bonus too.

345
00:50:10.409 --> 00:50:13.037
Everyone! Let's get going.

346
00:50:13.120 --> 00:50:16.165
We'll need to take a piss
and have some snacks on the way.

347
00:50:16.248 --> 00:50:18.918
We should leave now
if we want to make it in time.

348
00:50:19.418 --> 00:50:22.796
He's the one who wasted time
by taking a shit.

349
00:50:23.839 --> 00:50:26.342
Shut your mouth
and go start the car. punk.

350
00:50:26.425 --> 00:50:29.678
All right. Let's go now! Chop-chop!

351
00:50:30.930 --> 00:50:34.767
Let's go!

352
00:50:35.305 --> 00:51:35.904
